    "explanation_of_differences": "1. Row ID representation: Phase 1 stored 'original_index' as positional indices (198608 to 241165) after duplicate removal. Phase 2 assigns immutable 'row_id' tracking raw row positions in creditcard.csv (199324 to 242066).\n2. Within-timestamp tie-breaking: Phase 1 utilized unstable pandas quicksort on 'Time', causing local row permutation among transactions sharing identical timestamps. Phase 2 freezes stable raw row index ordering. The overall partition membership is 100% concordant, and validation metrics match Phase 1 exactly (AP: 0.650975, ROC-AUC: 0.947387)."
